\pard\sa120\sb120\fs32\b HPE ProLiant Windows Server ISO Automation (Root Readme)\b0{\*\bkmkstart hpe-proliant-windows-server-iso-automation-root-readme}{\*\bkmkend hpe-proliant-windows-server-iso-automation-root-readme}\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Summary\b0{\*\bkmkstart summary}{\*\bkmkend summary}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 Automated build pipelines for creating customized Windows Server installation ISOs and for orchestrating physical HPE ProLiant server deployments using Microsoft Configuration Manager bootable media, HPE OneView, and HPE iLO Redfish. Integrates firmware/driver updates, security patching, vulnerability scanning, complete audit trails, with OpsRamp monitoring and reporting.\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\brsp20\sa120\sb120\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b  Quick Start - Setup & Installation\b0{\*\bkmkstart quick-start-setup-installation}{\*\bkmkend quick-start-setup-installation}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 \b New to this project?\b0 Start here:\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 1. \b  Setup Guide\b0 - Complete setup instructions for PowerShell profile and maintenance mode 2. \b  Quick Client Setup\b0 - 5-minute setup for using maintenance mode commands\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b TL;DR - One-Line Setup\b0{\*\bkmkstart tldr-one-line-setup}{\*\bkmkend tldr-one-line-setup}\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2{\f1 make setup && . $PROFILE\f0}\par}
\pard\sa80\fs22 Then use:\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2{\f1 # 1. Connect to OneView and establish a persistent sessionConnect-OneView -ManagementHost oneview.example.com -Environment Prod# 2. Run OneView commands while the session is active# Get-OneViewServerList shows, per server: MaintMode (Yes/No), lifecycle State,# State Reason, Health, Power, iLO IP, ROM, and Model (HPE model code, last column).Get-OneViewServerListGet-OneViewConnectionStatus# 3. Disconnect from OneView when finishedDisconnect-OneView# 4. Enable maintenance modeSet-MaintenanceMode -Action enable -TargetId CLU-CLUSTER-01 -Mode scom -Environment Prod\f0}\par}
\pard\li360\ri360\sa80\fs22\i \b Tip - short parameter aliases:\b0 the OneView commands accept short aliases so they are faster to type. For example: {\f1 Get-OneViewConnectionStatus -SrvrId MXQ1234567 -IdTyp Serial\f0} is equivalent to {\f1 Get-OneViewConnectionStatus -ServerIdentifier MXQ1234567 -IdentifierType Serial\f0}. The long and short forms are interchangeable (see the Automation Command Reference for the full alias table).\i0\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2{\f1 # 5. Disable maintenance modeSet-MaintenanceMode -Action disable -TargetId CLU-CLUSTER-01 -Mode scom -Environment Prod\f0}\par}
