\pagebb\par\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b GitLab Pipeline Files\b0{\*\bkmkstart gitlab-pipeline-files}{\*\bkmkend gitlab-pipeline-files}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 The GitLab CI pipeline lives in {\f1 .gitlab-ci.yml\f0} at the repository root using PowerShell 7.4 containers.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b Pipeline Activation\b0{\*\bkmkstart pipeline-activation}{\*\bkmkend pipeline-activation}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 The pipeline is currently \b disabled\b0 via a workflow rule to prevent execution on the development GitLab instance. Before deploying to the Bank's GitLab:\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 1. Remove the {\f1 workflow\f0} block from {\f1 .gitlab-ci.yml\f0}:\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2{\f1  # Remove lines 9-13: # workflow: # rules: # - when: never\f0}\par}
\pard\sa80\fs22 1. Ensure {\f1 MAINTENANCE_API_KEY\f0} is configured as a masked variable in GitLab CI/CD settings 2. Verify all required secrets are configured in CyberArk for the bootstrap stage\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\brsp20\sa120\sb120\par
